MODULE 1 — JOB SEARCH ENGINE

Instructions:
- Accept the following search parameters from the user:
  * Job role / title (e.g., "Full Stack Developer", "Data Analyst", "Product Manager")
  * Required skills (comma-separated, e.g., "React, Node.js, AWS, Python")
  * Preferred location (city, state, country, or "Remote" / "Hybrid")
  * Years of experience (e.g., 3–6 years, 5+ years)
  * Expected salary/package range (e.g., ₹15–30 LPA or $80k–$120k)
  * Company name (optional — for targeted search)
  * Industry/domain (optional — e.g., FinTech, HealthTech, SaaS, E-commerce)

- Search the following job sources:
  * LinkedIn Jobs (use official LinkedIn Jobs API or structured search)
  * Naukri.com (use public search endpoints or official partner API)
  * Indeed (use Indeed Publisher API or structured queries)
  * Glassdoor (use Glassdoor API for job listings)
  * Company career pages (direct crawl of official /careers or /jobs pages where allowed)
  * AngelList / Wellfound (for startups)
  * Instahyre, Cutshort (for tech roles in India)
  * Google Jobs (via structured data / Google for Jobs API)

- For each source, retrieve:
  * Job title
  * Company name
  * Job location (city / remote / hybrid)
  * Date posted / last updated
  * Experience required
  * Salary/package (if visible)
  * Full job description text
  * Direct application URL

- Apply strict sourcing rules:
  * Use official APIs wherever available (LinkedIn, Indeed, Glassdoor all have APIs)
  * Never scrape websites that explicitly disallow scraping in their robots.txt
  * Never bypass login walls, CAPTCHA, OTP, or any authentication mechanism
  * For company career pages, only crawl pages that are publicly accessible
  * Respect rate limits and terms of service for all platforms

