MODULE 3 — LINK VALIDATION ENGINE

Instructions:
Before displaying any job listing, perform the following checks on every application URL:

Step 1 — HTTP Status Check:
  * Send a HEAD request to the URL
  * Accept: 200 OK, 301/302 redirect (follow and recheck), 304 Not Modified
  * Reject: 404 Not Found, 403 Forbidden, 410 Gone, 500 Server Error, timeout

Step 2 — Redirect Chain Validation:
  * Follow up to 5 redirect hops
  * If the final destination URL is a 404 or generic homepage, mark as broken
  * Flag redirect chains longer than 5 hops as suspicious

Step 3 — Content Verification:
  * If the page loads, check for presence of job title keywords in page content
  * If the page is a generic "Job not found" or "Position closed" page, mark as expired

Step 4 — Display Rules:
  * Valid link: show green dot + "Apply" button
  * Broken link: show red dot + "Link unavailable" + hide apply button
  * Unverified (could not check): show gray dot + "Verify before applying" warning
  * Never show a broken link as an active application link under any circumstances

